# Round qtq38: ik's CPU node dumps of the q38glue fixture variant (/models/fixture-variants/q38glue/qwen38: the Qwen3.8
# fixture with a Q4_K token embedding and a Q5_K head), the five Qwen3.8 fixture sets (batch, step4, step4-every-node, d1k,
# d3k), each one `BLOOMERY_TIER=fixture BLOOMERY_FIXTURE_VARIANT=q38glue just dump-ref-fixture qwen4exp [<set>]` under this
# card, one lease each. Nothing is timed.
# Minutes [derived]: the base fixture's Qwen3.8 dumps were 0.1 min for batch, step4 and step4-every-node, ~0.1 for d1k and
# 0.2-0.5 for d3k (docs/cards/fxoracle-dump.card, fxprobe's measured walls, Qwen3.8 4.4 s a batch), plus 3-15 s a lease take
# (0.25 min at the high end): 5 takes 0.3-1.3 min lease plus 0.6-1.0 min of dumps, 1..5 with the variant file paged in cold.
kind: exclusive
reason: dump_ref runs ik on 32 CPU threads and pages the variant file in, so it holds the lease; why now: gate-gpu-qwen4exp-e2e
  on the q38glue variant has no oracle sets until ik has dumped the variant, and the K-quant embedding rows and the Q5_K head
  are otherwise held only to our own graph = eager = pass clauses
minutes: 1..5
